# Line endings: keep the working tree LF everywhere.
#
# Why this file exists at all: the first public release build failed on GitHub Actions while the
# same command was green locally. The cause was not the code but the checkout — with
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows default, and what the runner had) git hands every text
# file back with CRLF, while the generators write LF. `tools/i18n-hant.mjs --check` then reported
# `generated.js is stale` for a file whose content was identical, and the release job stopped
# before it could build anything.
#
# Pinning the checkout to LF removes that whole class of "green here, red there": any byte
# comparison, hash or generated-artifact check now sees the same bytes on every machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched by the conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
